    "summary": "High‑energy ’69 set with soaring Dark Star, blistering Eleven and fierce Other One",
    "blurb": "The show opens with Good Morning Little School Girl before launching into a smoking Dark Star that segues into an intense The Eleven. A powerful Other One > Cryptical sequence follows, and Pigpen closes the night with Turn On Your Lovelight. Overall the performance is high‑energy and captured on two decent soundboard recordings.",
    "review": "The February 2, 1969 Labor Temple concert captures the Dead in a wild early‑'69 stride. Jerry Garcia’s lead work is dominant throughout – from the crystalline, soaring lines of Dark Star to the aggressive, post‑Schoolgirl fury that drives The Eleven into uncharted territory. The band rides that momentum straight into a fierce Other One > Cryptical pairing, with Tom Constanten’s keyboards adding texture under the twin‑drum thunder of Mickey and Billy. Pigpen’s soulful turn on Turn On Your Lovelight provides a satisfying, blues‑y climax to an otherwise psychedelic set. While both soundboard sources suffer from uneven mixes and occasional cuts, they remain among the better recordings of this era, preserving the raw intensity of a night when the Dead were locked in and unapologetically exploratory.",
